Ported (logic translated to Rust, not copied verbatim):

  src/ui/layout3d.c
    - directory ring seeding (FNV-1a cluster hash, 500 to 750 radius band)
    -> crates/kgraf-graph/src/layout.rs (cluster_center, cluster_key)
    - Z_DEPTH_SPACING and the call-depth walk
    -> crates/kgraf-graph/src/layout.rs (z_for, call_depths)
    - stellar_color, size_for_label, degree size boost
    -> crates/kgraf-graph/src/layout/stellar.rs

  graph-ui/src/lib/density.ts
    - edgeIntensityScale, bloomIntensityScale, nodeBoostScale, nodeGlowBoost
    -> crates/kgraf-graph/src/layout/density.rs

  graph-ui/src/components/EdgeLines.tsx, NodeCloud.tsx
    - edge intensity by cluster and selection, node dimming and scale
    -> crates/kgraf-graph/src/layout/density.rs

Not ported:

  src/ui/layout3d.c local_optimize (Barnes-Hut refinement with anchor spring),
  neither globally nor confined to one cluster. Globally it moves every
  existing node when one node is inserted, which breaks decision 0015; per
  cluster it moves every node of the cluster on each insert. Its spread is
  approximated instead by a disc whose radius grows with the cluster's
  population bucket (kGraf's own, not upstream's). Reasoning and
  measurements are in the module comment of
  crates/kgraf-graph/src/layout.rs.

Deviations from upstream behavior are listed in the same module comment.

